{"results":[{"id":"6ab561550075cd5f0b500b25","name":"The Not So Silent Miner: Threat Actor Compiles Cryptominer on the Endpoint","description":"A threat actor exploited a Samsung MagicINFO vulnerability (CVE-2025-4632) to gain initial access to victim endpoints. After three attempts, they successfully deployed a rogue AnyDesk instance using various download methods including certutil and PowerShell. The actor created a new local administrator account named 'oldadministrator' and disabled Microsoft Defender protections. Uniquely, instead of dropping a pre-compiled cryptominer, the threat actor compiled one directly on the compromised endpoint using Silent XMR Miner Builder.exe, executing multiple .NET Framework utilities and C compilers including donut.exe, tcc.exe, and MinGW64 tools. The resulting Monero cryptominer connected to the C3Pool mining service and ran under explorer.exe with suspicious command-line arguments. This compilation approach generated significant EDR telemetry, making the activity ironically conspicuous despite using tools associated with silent deployment.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-10-24T17:03:36.233000","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49.126000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4066090100,"indicator":"CVE-2024-7399","type":"CVE","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4071904017,"indicator":"CVE-2025-4632","type":"CVE","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4089624598,"indicator":"CVE-2025-47812","type":"CVE","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507109209,"indicator":"0d202e16408770e8b6cceb14e1e3e72946b154bf881d27fe33d0060315b30dd1","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507109211,"indicator":"http:\/\/194.87.89.30:8899\/anydesk.exe","type":"URL","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["c3pool","cryptominer","on-endpoint compilation","silentxmrminer","monero","cve-2024-7399","cve-2025-4632","anydesk","samsung magicinfo"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["SilentXMRMiner"],"attack_ids":["T1036.005","T1543.003","T1190","T1219","T1036","T1055","T1218","T1136.001","T1059.001","T1562.001","T1027","T1203","T1027.004","T1496","T1059.003","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/www.huntress.com\/blog\/threat-actor-compiles-cryptominer"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab561541d94721ef4ce040e","name":"RemotePanel and BoundSiphon: A Dual-Payload Toolkit for Persistent Access and Browser Theft","description":"Two previously undocumented .NET malware components were delivered through a ClickFix infection chain. RemotePanel establishes persistent remote access by masquerading as the Windows Time service, providing operators with PowerShell control, file and process management, screen access, modular HVNC, and fleet management capabilities. It uses a BNB Smart Chain contract to dynamically resolve its active Command and Control server, enabling infrastructure rotation without rebuilding the RAT. BoundSiphon runs primarily from memory, targeting browser credentials and sessions, cryptocurrency wallets, password manager data, and documents, including secrets protected by Chromium App-Bound Encryption. Strong code overlap exists between BoundSiphon and a stealer previously documented by Socket, linking the sample to an earlier stealer codebase. The modular design separates persistent access from data theft, allowing operators to replace infrastructure and individual components while maintaining operational capabilities.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-10-24T17:03:36.233000","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:48.732000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4494711212,"indicator":"greatgrgreeng.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4497845412,"indicator":"leftsideegpeakk.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507052351,"indicator":"30f9387b6aa2dd249d93cec58786251a224faaec57673a4b8104a33a01dfe62b","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507052352,"indicator":"351f0d27d2f0105186446693eed5794419ad79d7e6e647fc2fe74dbffb25f9ad","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507052353,"indicator":"5060c8184993d5ac04701ffa2c1d30451e40a7b2dbfc084eceaabb5084704991","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507052354,"indicator":"a7e8c9e157d3ce37913a32aaa861b5248da4cc5288fa99a6b291524af5e3b9c6","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507052355,"indicator":"b7a5c52cedd9cd5425a7f85b8d3b4b869b805c70c7991375a2c4ab612ff7906d","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4507052356,"indicator":"fec29bbd8e50b6635ef683f03f6e018c9627aa6362a2f167115424e50b8c1b10","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-09-24T17:43:49","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["credential theft","persistence","hvnc","remotepanel","app-bound encryption","boundsiphon","bnb smart chain","clickfix","browser hijacking","cryptocurrency wallet"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["RemotePanel","BoundSiphon"],"attack_ids":["T1113","T1033","T1539","T1548.002","T1204.002","T1573.001","T1543.003","T1082","T1005","T1140","T1555.003","T1134.002","T1083","T1041","T1059.001","T1056.002","T1562.001","T1055.012","T1071.001"],"references":["https:\/\/blackpointcyber.com\/blog\/remotepanel-and-boundsiphon-a-dual-payload-toolkit-for-persistent-access-and-browser-theft\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab4d79db2222977d275954f","name":"CARBONATO: a botnet built around an AI agent","description":"ThreatDown researchers discovered CARBONATO, a Docker botnet that exploits exposed Docker daemons on port 2375. The operation was uncovered through an unauthenticated Docker registry exposed since May 2026, revealing two parallel activities: distribution of trojanized cryptocurrency wallet applications and a botnet infrastructure. The botnet leverages Hermes Agent, an MIT-licensed open-source AI framework, modified with a custom prompt directing it to execute commands via Telegram, maintain persistence, and harvest credentials. The campaign infrastructure spans multiple hosting providers including Linode, Hetzner, and Contabo, with activity documented from October 2024 through August 2026.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-10-24T07:02:30.463000","created":"2026-09-24T07:56:13.523000","revision":3,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[],"tags":["cryptocurrency","credential theft","telegram","botnet","ai framework","carbonato","docker","hermes agent","container security","exposed daemon"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["CARBONATO","Hermes Agent"],"attack_ids":["T1543","T1133","T1071","T1053","T1140","T1190","T1555","T1567","T1219","T1552","T1090","T1102","T1204","T1072","T1027","T1573","T1132","T1111","T1136","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/www.threatdown.com\/blog\/carbonato\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ab51a43ec94931b637c0607","name":"Konni Hackers Target Ukraine With Malicious LNK Files and VelvetCake PowerShell Malware","description":"North Korea-linked threat actors are conducting Operation Conflict Compass, targeting individuals and organizations focused on Ukraine using spear-phishing emails with malicious ZIP attachments. These contain LNK files disguised as PDFs with themes related to Russia-Ukraine peace plans, Ukrainian research, and geopolitical issues. When executed, the shortcuts retrieve malicious files from GitHub, deploying VBScript to establish persistence via scheduled tasks and delivering VelvetCake, a lightweight PowerShell-based task runner. VelvetCake contacts command-and-control infrastructure to download and execute additional scripts that perform reconnaissance, collect system information, enumerate security software, and capture screenshots. The campaign also utilized trojanized Zoom installers and leveraged infrastructure in South Korea and Ukraine, with activity observed since early August 2026 targeting diplomatic entities, think tanks, and NGOs.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-10-24T00:01:02.963000","created":"2026-09-24T12:40:35.284000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Opal Sleet","indicators":[{"id":4503562613,"indicator":"p1o2i3u4y5t6r7e8w9q0.medianewsonline.com","type":"hostname","created":"2026-09-24T12:40:36","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["operation conflict compass","scheduled tasks","ukraine targeting","lnk files","north korea","spear-phishing","velvetcake","powershell"],"targeted_countries":["Ukraine"],"malware_families":["VelvetCake"],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/cyberpress.org\/konni-targets-ukraine-with-velvetcake\/"],"industries":["Government","NGO"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6adb52fde8bfb072942ad917","name":"VeloCloud Orchestrator SQL Injection Vulnerability","description":"VeloCloud Orchestrator (VCO) on-premises versions contain a critical SQL injection vulnerability that allows authenticated users with minimal privileges to escalate to superuser operator access. Any user with Enterprise Read Only role can exploit this flaw to access privileged internal functionality, potentially compromising the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the orchestrator and managed data. The vulnerability is actively exploited, with specific malicious IP addresses identified. Affected versions include VCO 5.2.x prior to 5.2.3.18, 6.1.x prior to 6.1.3.10, and 6.4.x prior to 6.4.2.12. Hosted and dedicated VCO instances were already patched. Immediate upgrade to fixed releases is recommended, along with restricting web interface access and monitoring for suspicious activity.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-10-23T12:29:52.147000","created":"2026-10-23T12:28:45.765000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4542979069,"indicator":"74.82.197.86","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-10-23T12:29:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-11-22T00:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4542979070,"indicator":"38.54.50.151","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-10-23T12:28:46","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-11-22T12:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4542979071,"indicator":"CVE-2026-114625","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-23T12:28:46","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["sql injection","active exploitation","velocloud orchestrator","cve-2026-114625"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1133","T1082","T1071","T1190","T1595.002","T1505.003","T1548","T1210","T1098","T1078","T1068","T1046"],"references":["https:\/\/www.arista.com\/en\/support\/advisories-notices\/security-advisory\/24838-security-advisory-0199"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ada6051fb91aa7551af4ba6","name":"SEO Poisoning Campaign Delivers New Armorsteal Malware","description":"In September 2026, an SEO poisoning campaign distributed Armorsteal malware through fake websites impersonating Chocolatey package manager and Microsoft Activation Scripts (MAS) tool. Victims searching for software installation commands were presented with malicious PowerShell scripts that deployed Python-based malware protected by Pyarmor. The malware consists of three main components: a remote access module that communicates with command-and-control servers and verifies RSA-2048 signatures on received tasks; a surveillance module that logs keystrokes, monitors clipboard activity, hijacks cryptocurrency wallet addresses, and captures screenshots; and an information stealer targeting browser data, Discord tokens, cryptocurrency wallets, seed phrases, passwords, and SSH keys. The campaign employed anti-analysis techniques including cloud provider detection and code obfuscation, with infrastructure changes observed throughout the monitoring period.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-10-23T12:25:30.997000","created":"2026-10-22T19:13:21.613000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":3457594533,"indicator":"186.2.163.185","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-10-22T19:13:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-11-21T19:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":3467620461,"indicator":"190.115.31.69","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-10-22T19:13:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-11-21T19:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4497935176,"indicator":"massgravel.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-22T19:13:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4543043632,"indicator":"186.2.175.183","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-10-22T19:13:22","content":"","title":"","descrip